🏗️ Architecture Summary

Backend: FastAPI (Python 3.12+)
Frontend: React + TypeScript + Vite
Database: PostgreSQL
Cache: Redis
Queue: Celery
APIs: YouTube Data v3, Analytics v2
LLM: GPT-4 / Gemini

backend/ → api, models, services, db, core
frontend/ → components, pages, services, types.ts


⸻

💻 Coding Rules

Python
	•	Add type hints, use async/await, follow PEP 8, and use Google-style docstrings.
	•	Use logger, not print.
	•	Handle errors with try/except and HTTPException.
	•	Keep business logic in services/, not in routes.

TypeScript
	•	Enable strict mode.
	•	Use interfaces, async/await, and try/catch.
	•	Components must be ≤ 300 lines, functional, and use hooks.
	•	All API calls go in frontend/services/.

⸻

🗄️ Database
	•	Create Alembic migrations only when schema changes.
	•	Add indexes on foreign keys and frequently queried columns.
	•	Keep models pure — no business logic.

⸻

🔌 API
	•	Follow RESTful conventions.
	•	Use correct HTTP verbs and consistent JSON responses.
	•	Raise HTTPException with descriptive messages.

⸻

🎨 Frontend
	•	One component per file, typed props.
	•	Reuse logic via custom hooks.
	•	Style using Tailwind CSS (mobile-first).
	•	Remove all console.log from production.

⸻

🔄 Celery
	•	Tasks must be idempotent.
	•	Use retry with exponential backoff.
	•	Log key progress points.
	•	Return structured dicts: { success, data, error }.

⸻

🔐 Security
	•	Use OAuth 2.0 for YouTube.
	•	Encrypt stored tokens.
	•	Validate user/channel ownership.
	•	Protect routes with Depends(get_current_user).

⸻

📊 Logging
	•	Use structured logging with levels: DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, ERROR.
	•	Log:
	•	Requests/responses
	•	Worker task lifecycle
	•	External API calls
	•	Errors and timing

⸻

🧪 Testing
	•	Use pytest.
	•	Mock external APIs.
	•	Cover error paths and edge cases.

⸻

🚀 Performance
	•	Use async I/O and connection pooling.
	•	Add DB indexes, cache heavy ops (Redis).
	•	Frontend: lazy load, memoize, code split.

⸻

📦 Dependencies

Backend:

pip install pkg==ver
pip freeze | grep pkg >> requirements.txt

Frontend:

npm install pkg@ver

	•	Avoid bloat; prefer stdlib and maintained packages.

⸻

🔧 Environment
	•	Add all new vars to .env.example.
	•	Never commit real .env files.

⸻

✅ Review Checklist
	•	Type hints / interfaces
	•	Error handling + logging
	•	Indexes (if needed)
	•	Endpoint tested
	•	Responsive UI
	•	No prints/logs in prod
	•	Docs updated only if major change

⸻

🚫 Anti-Patterns

Backend: print(), blocking I/O, missing type hints, hardcoded values, logic in routes.
Frontend: inline API calls, no loading/error states, prop drilling, unused imports, missing types.

⸻

💡 Best Practices
	•	DRY, clear naming, small focused functions.
	•	Use caching, pagination, and batch operations.
	•	Handle YouTube API rate limits gracefully.
	•	Always test with edge cases.

⸻

